== Problem description ==
Face ID stops working because the TrueDepth sensor module is shorted.

This is most often caused by:

* Water damage
* Accidental damage while the device is open during other repairs (e.g., display replacement, battery replacement etc.)

== Symptoms ==

* Settings → About → Parts & Service History → “Issue with Face ID detected”
* Unable to set up Face ID
* Face ID unavailable
[[File:Unable-to-setup-faceid.png|thumb|Unable to setup Face ID]]
== Diagnostic Steps ==

# Attempt to set up Face ID in Settings → Face ID & Passcode.
# Confirm history of water damage or previous repair work with the customer.
# Inspect the TrueDepth module for visible damage or corrosion.

== Repair Steps ==

# Open the iPhone and disconnect/remove the TrueDepth camera module.
# Power on the phone without the module connected and connect it to a PC.
# Open JC Repair Assistant on the PC and connect a JC V1S Pro or V1SE programmer. [You will need [https://www.diyfixtool.com/products/jcid-iphone-13-16-face-id-repair-tag-on-fpc-activation-board?srsltid=AfmBOoqwf36a-mVB3p8K7Fh2yab9pB1hK2pTHb8EGty47QR_I6QD_2bo&variant=47556754473189 13-16 Series Face ID Activation / Read & Write Adaptor]]
# Perform a cloud backup of the TrueDepth module data using JC software.
# Test TrueDepth module and confirm module fuses.[[File:Abnormal-faced.png|center|thumb|Face ID showing Fused]]
# Click Activate and wait until the process completes.
# Connect the respective Tag-on flex cable to the JC programmer.
# Write the corresponding device Face ID data onto the flex from the backup.
# Verify that the flex shows the original TrueDepth data.
# Connect the Tag-on flex to the TrueDepth module and recheck in JC software/programmer: Should now show “NORMAL” instead of “FUSED”.[[File:Normal-faceid.png|center|thumb|Face ID Normal]]
# Fold the Tag-on flex according to your iPhone model (follow JC’s reference videos).
# Reinstall the TrueDepth module with the Tag-on flex attached.
# Power on the phone and verify that Face ID is fully functional.[[File:Face-id-success.png|center|thumb|Face ID successfully setup]]